+# US-28: Integration and system tests
+
+| | |
+| --- | --- |
+| Epic | Quality / Test Plan section 13 |
+| Requirement | Test Plan 13; verifies MLE-F-007, MLE-F-008, MLE-F-009, MLE-NF-006, MLE-SR-006 |
+| Points / sprint | 5 / Sprint 2 |
+| Owner | Varnika (Member 2) |
+
+**Story.** As a developer I want tests that run the real pieces together, so that I find faults that unit tests of single services cannot.
+
+## Levels
+
+| Level | File | What is real | Count |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Unit (US-11) | `test_services_unit.py` and others | One service at a time | 139+ |
+| Integration | `test_integration.py` | HTTP layer, validation, database, job runner, artifact storage, limits, **a separate training process** | 6 |
+| System | `test_system.py` | Black-box journeys over HTTP only: log in, use the API, read the result | 4 |
+
+## Integration tests
+
+- Every catalogue model's defaults pass validation and train to a stored model.
+- A stored model predicts on the user's own test split (better than chance).
+- An invalid hyperparameter never creates a job.
+- Two users are fully separated (runs, folders, 404 on the other's run).
+- A crashed job, then a good job: the failure frees the student's slot.
+- Limits sit in front of training (a student at quota is refused; becoming a Data Scientist allows a second job).
+- A real background thread finishes a job after the request has already returned.
+
+## System tests (TC-MODEL-01 and neighbours)
+
+- Journey: not logged in (401) -> log in -> list models -> bad C refused with the exact message -> good C accepted -> train -> completed with the chosen parameters.
+- Wrong password (401), logout blocks further use.
+- A student double-clicking Train: the first job runs, the second is refused (429), a new one is allowed after the first ends.
+- Hostile input (broken JSON, wrong types, SQL-looking text, wrong methods) gets clean 4xx errors, never a 500.
+
+## Result
+
+**202 tests pass** (3 slower performance tests run separately with `-m perf`).
+
+## Defects found while writing them
+
+- The sample-data accuracy threshold in my first draft was wrong (classes overlap); fixed in the test, not the code.
+- A test left a job running when the test database was removed (test teardown race); the test now waits for its job.
+- No product defects were found at this level; the earlier ones (NaN `test_size`, sparse-matrix slowness) were found by US-11 and US-20.
